tesman of Circassian origin.", "newValue": "Hafız Mehmed Paşa, a distinguished Ottoman military officer and statesman of Circassian origin, rose through the ranks to hold significant administrative and military positions in the mid-19th century, a period defined by the Ottoman Empire's ambitious Tanzimat reforms and escalating geopolitical pressures. Born into an era of profound transformation, his career, culminating in his death on May 3, 1866, encapsulated the challenges and opportunities faced by a modernizing empire striving to consolidate its authority and adapt to European military and administrative standards.

